   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- Reviewer singled out the run of Springtheme, Monique the Freak and Fluffy as the best sequence of the night [5]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Cover It With Gas and Set It on Fire**: back after 58 archived shows (2385 days) [6]\n- **I'll Miss You**: rare: 14 archived performances [6]\n- **Sweet Texas Fire**: back after 58 archived shows (2385 days) [6]\n- **There's a Pig**: back after 87 archived shows (2871 days); rare: 5 archived performances [6]\n- **Sunday Morning Coming Down**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- **I'm Holding You**: back after 186 archived shows (4209 days) [6]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **ween2017-06-11.ck61.nbox.mp6.flac** (recommended): source not stated; 32 songs; 143 min; rated 5/5 by 2 [1]\n- **WN2017-06-11.24bit**: source not stated; 32 songs; 144 min [2]\n- **WN2017-06-11.16bit**: source not stated; 32 songs; 144 min [3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Reviewer attended in person and says the band impressed them, with many high points, despite finding the setlist weak on paper [5]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **ween2017-06-11.ck61.nbox.mp6.flac**: taped by Ted Gakidis; transferred by Ted Gakidis; source: AKG CK61 Actives(DIN,FOB) > nBox > Sound Devices Mixpre-6 (24/48) [1]\n- **WN2017-06-11.24bit**: taped by StarkRavingCalm; transferred by StarkRavingCalm; source: AKG CK-63 > Tascam DR-60D [2]\n- **WN2017-06-11.16bit**: taped by StarkRavingCalm; transferred by StarkRavingCalm; source: AKG CK-63 > Tascam DR-60D [3]",
